H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"7ed5d2dd5c084ba3bfcf686878c5027be31d03aa98131a1c3f751b137626f61f","event_uuid":"184dbb8d-39c8-4f32-9ef6-b79729978b51","position":{"commit_sha":"7d1365d49cc4e1bac9018c1c10daa443b0e37318","position":"1789945790999272118-184dbb8d-39c8-4f32-9ef6-b79729978b51"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Repriced P1 → P4, and the description rewritten\n\nThis ticket was filed at P1 claiming a signing-correctness hole in which a `completion-verifier` signature could be minted over a stale tree. That claim was not supported by any observation. It was inferred from reading the source, and then written up with a severity and a store-wide census attached to substantiate it.\n\nThe investigation that produced the reading had already stated the hedge correctly — \"the mechanism for a signed false PASS is demonstrated; an actual instance is not\" — and the hedge was dropped when the ticket was written.\n\nWhat is actually on the record: one incident, on `8806-198c-e2d6-46ce`, which was a false FAIL. The verifier could not see work that had merged. That is the safe direction, and it is the opposite of the failure this ticket asserted.\n\nA further gap the original draft did not acknowledge: it was never established what the post-verify drift check is *for*. If its purpose is to detect the tree moving during verification, then comparing the pin against itself across that window is the intended behaviour and there is no defect at all. Settling that costs a reading of the check's intent, and it comes before anything else here.\n\nThe census is now out of scope. Inventing expensive work to substantiate an unobserved hypothesis is the thing that went wrong, not a remedy for it.","timestamp":1789785261996856478}],"created_at":1789784902618078892,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"08d7ad79-9931-4b76-881c-2a62053cc0c0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8806-198c-e2d6-46ce"},{"link_uuid":"a004d3d2-ac75-4508-933f-19dde98a1904","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7d60-efed-61dc-4711"},{"link_uuid":"8ad14f5d-c01e-4736-a714-03ca88e329b6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dd99-f0c0-8860-440e"},{"link_uuid":"184dbb8d-39c8-4f32-9ef6-b79729978b51","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7076-0b5d-b159-494a"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n**Status: the reading is CONFIRMED by executable demonstration, but the defect is narrower\nthan the title supposes.** The pre-sign drift guard does re-resolve its own pin — however\nthat pinning is *intentional and tested*, so the code is right. What is wrong is\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md`, which documents a live-HEAD drift check that the default close\npath can no longer reach.\n\nThis ticket is therefore a **documentation correction**, not a behavioural change.\n\n## Root cause — established by measurement\n\n`close_ticket` pins the completion target **once, at close entry**\n(`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:505`, via `_pin_completion_ref`), resolving both\nan explicit `--ref` *and the default `HEAD`* down to a concrete SHA without fetching\n(`transition_close.py:128`, `:140`, `:142`). That pinned ref is threaded through the\nauto-resume wrapper to verification (`src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py:211-213`,\n`:271`, `:275-276`).\n\nThe pre-sign guard then reads `verified-at-sha` from the manifest and, when `ref` is present\nand not the literal string `\"HEAD\"`, calls `resolve_ref(ref, ..., fetch=False)` **again**\n(`transition_close.py:297`, `:312`, `:320`). Because `ref` is by then already a full SHA,\nthat is a self-comparison and can never report drift. The only branch that reads live HEAD\nis the `ref=None` fallback (`transition_close.py:322`) — and after the entry pin, `ref` is\nnever `None`.\n\n### Executable demonstration\n\nA scratch pytest exercised both paths directly, with no LLM call and no live gate:\n\n```\nPINNED pin=154b75956ef0 head_after=c1c91c36ee4f\n       outcome={'signed': True,  'cause': 'signed'}\nLIVE   verified=154b75956ef0 head_after=c1c91c36ee4f\n       outcome={'signed': False, 'cause': 'material_drifted'}\n2 passed in 1.37s\n```\n\nSame verified SHA, same subsequent HEAD move. With the pre-resolved pin it signs; with\n`ref=None` it correctly refuses as `material_drifted`. That is the mechanism, isolated.\n\n## Why the code is correct and must not change\n\nPinning is deliberate, and there is already a committed test asserting it:\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_symbolic_ref_pins_3e21.py` (`3 passed in 7.95s`)\nasserts that a concurrent `origin/main` move still lands **signed**, bound to the originally\nverified SHA.\n\nThat is the right semantic. An attestation should certify **the commit that was actually\nverified**, not whatever HEAD happens to be at signing time. Re-resolving to live HEAD would\neither attest a tree the verifier never saw, or spuriously refuse a close because an\nunrelated change landed during the 9-11 minute gate run. Both are worse than pinning.\n\n## The actual defect\n\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md` ends its `--ref` paragraph with:\n\n> Absent `--ref`, behavior is unchanged (verify at HEAD, drift-check against `head_sha`).\n\nBoth halves of the parenthetical are now false. Absent `--ref` the close **pins HEAD to a\nSHA at entry** and then drift-checks that SHA against itself, so it does not \"drift-check\nagainst `head_sha`\" in any meaningful sense — the guard is inert on that path.\n\nThe cost of the stale sentence is real: it tells a reader that an unpinned close is\nprotected against the base moving mid-gate, so a reader debugging a stale-looking\nattestation will look for a guard failure that structurally cannot occur.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Correct the stale sentence in `docs/plan-review-gate.md` to state what the code does:\n   the default path pins HEAD at close entry, and the resulting attestation certifies that\n   pinned commit rather than live HEAD at signing time. Name the observable consequence —\n   `verified_at_sha` may be older than current HEAD, and that is correct, not drift.\n2. Keep the existing `--ref` explanation, which is accurate.\n3. Add a test pinning the documented default-path behaviour, so the doc and the code cannot\n   drift apart again silently. The demonstration above is already most of that test.\n\n### Rejected\n\n- **Making the default path drift-check live HEAD.** This would contradict\n  `test_close_symbolic_ref_pins_3e21.py` and would make any close racing an unrelated merge\n  fail spuriously. The pin is the feature.\n- **Deleting the `ref=None` branch as dead code.** It is reachable by direct library callers\n  that bypass `close_ticket`'s pinning, and it is the correct behaviour for them.\n- **Closing this as \"works as intended\" with no change.** The doc is materially wrong and\n  actively misleads; leaving it costs the next reader an investigation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The sentence \"Absent `--ref`, behavior is unchanged (verify at HEAD, drift-check\n  against `head_sha`)\" no longer appears in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, replaced by text that\n  correctly describes entry-time pinning. Verified by `grep -n 'drift-check against' docs/`\n  returning no stale match.\n- [ ] The replacement text states the user-observable consequence: a completion\n  attestation's `verified_at_sha` can legitimately be older than current HEAD.\n- [ ] A test asserts the default-path behaviour — that a close whose HEAD moves after the\n  entry pin still lands **signed**, bound to the pinned SHA — so the documented claim has a\n  code oracle. Verified by the new test passing, and by it failing if the pin is removed.\n- [ ] `test_close_symbolic_ref_pins_3e21.py` still passes unchanged, confirming the existing\n  contract was not disturbed.\n- [ ] No change to `transition_close.py` behaviour. Verified by the diff touching no\n  production logic, or by explicit justification if it must.\n\n## Testing\n\n```\ngrep -n 'drift-check against' docs/\npython -m pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_symbolic_ref_pins_3e21.py -p no:randomly -q\n```\n\nThe first must return no stale match; the second must stay at 3 passed. The new\ndefault-path test must pass with the pin in place and fail without it, so it is a regression\noracle rather than a restatement of current behaviour.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7076-0b5d-b159-494a"],["relates_to","7d60-efed-61dc-4711"],["relates_to","dd99-f0c0-8860-440e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cf9a85ce-342d-41ef-9753-b41733f09e35","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":4,"repos":[],"reverts":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","reason":"un-archive via transition archived open","target_event_type":"ARCHIVED","target_event_uuid":"66d4751a-ed6e-4868-9499-531d58908562","timestamp":1789785145972648001,"uuid":"64793591-d218-46db-bd3e-6727feacb916"}],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a2e5-094d-0736-456e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Unverified reading: the completion close drift check may re-resolve its own pin, and its intended scope is unestablished","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["66d4751a-ed6e-4868-9499-531d58908562","64793591-d218-46db-bd3e-6727feacb